--- commit message of head
KS-835: an OAuth-minted token carries the scopes the user GRANTED and an 'oauth' label, so the gateway gates it on the grant

The consent screen asked the user to approve a list of scopes and the token
that came out ignored it. The chain: /authorize computed and stored the granted
scopes; the token grant minted with generateTokenPair(user, session.id) -- the
grant was not a parameter -- so the `scopes` claim came from
getDefaultScopesForRole(user.role) (the user's ROLE), and no label
distinguished an OAuth-minted token from the user's own browser login; the
gateway's requireScope short-circuits every token whose authMethod is missing /
'jwt' / 'email'. A third-party app approved for `openid` received a token
carrying the user's full role-derived authority.

THE THREE HYPOTHESES, RUN AGAINST THE UNFIXED PRODUCT FIRST (the ticket's bar):
- H1 the mint has no scope parameter: an OWNER approving `openid` got a token
  whose scopes read ["documents:write"] (the role default). RED, measured.
- H2 the label: the minted token carried no authMethod. RED, measured.
- H3 the dead bridge: the gateway's attachScopes parsed a singular `scope`
  claim nothing mints. Measured as "reads a claim that does not exist", not as
  a broken gate: authenticateToken puts the verified claims on req.user as-is,
  so a `scopes` array and an 'oauth' label ARE read by requireScope today --
  the gateway gates that shape already; nothing minted it.

THE FIX (the mint):
- jwt.ts: OAuthMintOptions gains `scopes` (required -- every OAuth mint states
  its grant); OAuthTokenClaims gains `authMethod?: 'oauth'`; an OAuth mint puts
  `scopes` = the granted list (even when empty: nothing granted, nothing
  allowed) and `authMethod: 'oauth'` on both halves of the pair; a login mint is
  UNCHANGED (no label, role-default scopes -- RBAC governs those).
- oauth.ts: the code grant passes parseScopeString(result.scope) -- validated
  against the app's allow-list at /authorize -- so the response's informational
  `scope` now describes the token it accompanies; the refresh grant re-mints the
  token's OWN granted scopes, never widening back to the role default.
- api-gateway scopes.ts: attachScopes documented honestly -- the array arrives
  on the token and is left alone; the singular-string parse is the RFC 6749 3.3
  wire form nothing here mints, a compatibility arm that runs only when no
  array is present and never widens a grant. No behaviour change.

BLAST RADIUS, stated: after deploy, every NEW OAuth token is gated by its grant
at the eight requireScope mounts (RBAC-only routes are unchanged); OAuth ACCESS
tokens minted before deploy carry no label and keep the bypass until they
expire (JWT_EXPIRES_IN bounds it); OAuth REFRESH tokens minted before deploy are
already refused by the client-binding change this branch stacks on, so nothing
pre-deploy re-mints unlabelled. Which deployed clients hold OAuth tokens today
is UNMEASURED (the ticket's own line) and stays so.

Tests (vitest run, node v24.7.0, darwin):
- services/auth NEW ks835-oauth-mint-carries-granted-scope.test.ts (5 cells,
  raw socket, real jwt.ts): red-first at the parent commit `Tests 4 failed |
  1 passed (5)` -- H1 ["documents:write"] where ["openid"] belongs, H2 label
  undefined, the refresh re-mint and the empty grant likewise; the login-shape
  control green. Green 5/5 after.
- services/api-gateway NEW ks835-oauth-token-scope-gate.test.ts (6 cells,
  RS256 tokens in the claim shape jwt.ts mints, real authenticateToken →
  attachScopes → requireScope on a listener): narrow 'oauth' token -> 403
  naming granted; the same with the scope granted -> 200; an sk_* key with the
  narrow scope -> 403 (the gate, not the OAuth path, refuses); an UNLABELLED
  token with narrow scopes -> 200 (the mechanism the ticket named, pinned as
  the login rule); 'oauth' with no scopes -> 403; attachScopes' two arms.
  Green before AND after -- controls: the gate already discriminated on the
  label; the mint did not produce it. The cross-service assertion (one token
  minted in auth, gated in the gateway) is by claim-name convention across the
  two files, NOT a single run -- stated in both.
- Whole auth suite 53 files / 707 tests (was 52 / 702 on the parent); whole
  gateway suite 35 files / 349 tests (unchanged count +6 -- 343 before). tsc rc 0
  in both services; the new test files type-checked separately rc 0.
- Tampers (restored by content, sha asserted): T1 the access-token mint drops
  the granted scopes -> 3 red (H1; refresh; empty grant); T2 the label dropped
  -> 3 red (H2; refresh; empty grant -- predicted 2, the empty-grant cell also
  asserts the label); T3 the refresh re-mint widened to the role default -> 1
  red; T4 the code grant mints the role default -> 3 red. All reds are the
  named cells.
- ks823-refresh-grant-client-auth-and-binding.test.ts (this lane's, stacked):
  its mint helper states a grant, as the option type now requires; assertions
  unchanged.

Not covered: a live token through the real gateway; the four platform suites;
which deployed clients hold OAuth tokens today.

